@startuml
title Git Flow — Création d'une Pull Request (GitHub)

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor Black
  ActorBorderColor Black
  ParticipantBorderColor Black
  LifeLineBorderColor Black
  LifeLineBackgroundColor White
}

actor Dev as "Développeur"
participant Local as "Repo local (git)"
participant Remote as "GitHub (origin)"
participant CI as "CI/CD"
actor Reviewer as "Reviewer"
actor Maintainer as "Mainteneur"

== Préparation ==
Dev -> Local: git checkout -b feature/ma-fonction
note right of Local
  Branches:
  - main (production)
  - develop (optionnel - Git Flow)
  - feature/ma-fonction
end note

Dev -> Local: Coder, tester en local

loop Commits incrémentaux
  Dev -> Local: git add . && git commit -m "Message clair"
end

== Publication ==
Dev -> Remote: git push -u origin feature/ma-fonction

== Pull Request ==
Dev -> Remote: Ouvrir PR: feature/ma-fonction -> main\n(lier issue, ajouter description)
Remote -> CI: Déclenche checks (tests, lint, build)
CI --> Remote: Statuts des checks

== Revue ==
Reviewer -> Remote: Revue, commentaires, approbations
alt Changements demandés
  Dev -> Local: Corriger
  Dev -> Local: commit
  Dev -> Remote: push
  Remote -> CI: Relance checks
  CI --> Remote: OK
else OK pour merge
  Reviewer -> Remote: Approve
end

== Merge ==
Maintainer -> Remote: Merge (Merge/Squash/Rebase)
note over Remote
  Historique propre recommandé: Squash
end note
Remote --> Dev: PR = Merged
Dev -> Local: git checkout main && git pull --ff-only
Dev -> Remote: Supprimer branche feature

@enduml